The '''Autopista AP-1''' (also '''AP-1''', more popularly known as '''Autopista del Mar'''; {{Literal translation|Sea Motorway}}) is a major north–south [[Autopista of Balisca|Baliscan autopista]] route that runs along most of the [[Levante, Balisca|Atlantic coastline]] of the [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Hesperia]]. At {{convert|1605.04|km|mi}}, it is the longest route in Hesperia, and the [[List of longest autopista in Balisca|second-longest in Balisca]] after [[tba]]. AP-1 has several portions designated as either '''Atlantic Coast Highway''' ('''ACH'''), '''Hesperian Highway''', or '''Coast Highway'''. Its southern terminus is at [[Orquívoro]] in [[Piedmont]] and its northern terminus is at [[Cordova]] in [[Basilisco]]. 

AP-1 was built piecemeal in various stages, with the first section opening in the [[Acacias]] region in the 1920s. However, portions of the route had several names and numbers over the years as more segments opened. Although AP-1 is a popular route for its scenery, frequent landslides, erosion and [[W:South Atlantic tropical cyclone|South Atlantic tropical cyclones]] along the coast have caused several segments to be either closed for lengthy periods for repairs, or re-routed inland.{{Balisca articles}}
